{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["וּבְקָעֵהוּ — the ayin causes the doubling. Like ״שְׁמָעֵנוּ אדוני״, but from זכור it says זָכְרֵנִי."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Rashbam explains that theע in וּבְקָעֵהוּ triggers a dagesh-like doubling in the following consonant (a pi'el imperative with heavy ayin), contrasting it with forms like זָכְרֵנִי where no such doubling occurs."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:27.584662260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}